The (approximately) shortest reproducer of this bug is:
```
int table[256];
int foo(signed char x) {
  unsigned char y = x;
  if (x >= 0)
    return x;
  return table[y];
}
```
I created PR https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/127062 which adds this (and two related cases) to the tests of the analyzer to highlight and document that this problem exists.

I'll probably create a "duct tape" commit that silences most of the the `security.ArrayBound` false positives caused by this bug.

