It looks like `ScalarExprEmitter::VisitCastExpr` isn't resigning the pointer.

```
case CK_NoOp: {
    return CE->changesVolatileQualification() ? EmitLoadOfLValue(CE)
                                              : Visit(const_cast<Expr *>(E));
  }
```

`E` is the subexpression of the `ImplicitCastExpr`.

Another interesting case:

```c++
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdarg.h>

void NoexceptFunction() noexcept {
    printf("NE function\n");
}

[[gnu::noinline]]
void CallThroughThrowingFnPointer(int dummy, ...) {
    va_list args;
    va_start(args, dummy);
    auto* fn = va_arg(args, void(*)()); // non-noexcept function pointer
    fn();
    va_end(args);
}

int main() {
    CallThroughThrowingFnPointer(0, &NoexceptFunction); // no resigning code generated here (compiler can't know how the argument will be used)
}
```

