Oh, I must have made a typo when I was trying out `module : private;` earlier today, I see it working now when I test again. I could probably also work around this problem by using module partitions for some of my more problematic modules.

My expectation for how the private module fragment would interact with my example is that `module a` could instead be defined as

```cpp
export module a;

#define REPEAT8(x) \
	(x), \
	(x), \
	(x), \
	(x), \
	(x), \
	(x), \
	(x), \
